# iCaNova Monitoring — architecture

## Product & boundaries

- Platform: **iCaNova Monitoring**. Edge companion: **iCaNova Edge Gateway**.
- Terminology: `docs/product/terminology.md`. Do not invent brand/product names.
- Auth/env identifiers stay as-is unless a migration is approved.
- Web owns UI, Convex Auth/authz, org/site/device/telemetry presentation, alarms, notifications, deployment tooling.
- Keep hardware/Modbus specifics out of the frontend. Keep presentation out of firmware.
- Backend authorization stays on the backend. Preserve explicit gateway↔cloud contracts.
- Do not duplicate an existing responsibility without architectural justification.

## System rules

- Org-scoped Convex (`convex/`) + React SPA (`src/`). Fail closed on auth misconfig.
- Prefer shared components (`src/ui/`, `src/sites/`) over page-local copies.
- Live data via Convex subscriptions — no full-page reload for refresh.
- Keep cloud contact, Modbus/link health, and measurement freshness **separate**.
- Do not invent telemetry fields the backend does not store.
- Smallest safe change. No drive-by refactors. CSS mobile overrides **after** base rules.

## Hard gates

- No unauthorized production deploy (`sturgeon`) or production secret changes.
- No destructive Convex wipes/migrations without explicit owner approval + recovery plan.
- Do not flash hardware or open serial ports from this repo’s tasks.

## Verify before claiming done

1. Inspect actual UI/state (browser, tests, or computed evidence) — not code alone.
2. Confirm the reported viewport/environment.
3. Run relevant tests; if skipped, say why.
4. After **substantial** work, end with the mandatory completion report (11 sections in `verification-and-testing.mdc`).
